e becomes possible because now  the rook has no control of the h7 square  so yeah after knight to f6 tari resigned  the game and  what a brilliant attacking game by  magnus carlsen really not  much happened there uh it was simply a  matter of  exploiting a better position to the  maximum  magnets having a beautiful monster  knight and the five tari having a dark  square bishop and his  pawns were also on dark squares so it  was incredibly hard  for him to to even make moves at this  game uh but yeah uh quite a game uh here  for those of you who  still uh haven't seen the standings or  for some reason don't remember the  standings  uh here they are magnus in first place  with 16 and a half points followed by  alireza ferrugia  and here we're going to have an  incredible clash in round nine because  we have carlson versus ferugia  and uh carlson won their previous uh  previous game  uh in uh in the first part of the  tournament now alex has a chance to  the strike back uh we'll see what  happens as the the battle for the future  continues  then we have 11 aaron in third place  fabiano carwana in fourth young shisht  of dudain in fifth and  arientari still on point and a half uh  in sixth place  but you know it's not easy rolling it  out with these monsters here  uh uh that's uh that's the game uh i do  hope you enjoyed it uh i would like to  thank  milan simon johansson srivastava  uh raymond young and the dustin jonatha  for contribution to my channel  thank you a lot i really appreciate it  uh as usual you can check to my previous  videos here thank you for watching and i  will see you soon  uh continuing uh of course this very  short coverage of the  ultimate snowy championship checking up  on your wonderful suggestions and  whatever else happens in the chess world  so thank you all i will see you soon and  have an excellent rest of your day next  game is  firuja vs carlson uh see you soon
 

